# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored and must stay that way. This repository is public, and a
# leaked bot token lets anyone read the channels the bot can see. If one is
# ever committed, reset it in the Developer Portal rather than deleting the
# commit — a pushed secret is a public secret.
#
# This file holds no values, only names, so it is safe to commit.


# --- Discord ----------------------------------------------------------------

# Developer Portal -> your application -> Bot -> Reset Token.
# Shown once. If you lose it, reset again; that invalidates the old one.
#
# On that same page, switch on Message Content Intent under Privileged Gateway
# Intents. It is off by default, and the symptom of forgetting is empty message
# text with no error anywhere.
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=

# Right-click your server icon -> Copy Server ID.
# Needs Settings -> Advanced -> Developer Mode switched on first.
# Used to build the permanent post link, not to find the channel.
GUILD_ID=

# Right-click the news channel -> Copy Channel ID.
# The channel your server follows the Pokémon GO news channel into.
CHANNEL_ID=

# Optional. Right-click one existing post -> Copy Message ID.
#
# Read only on the very first run, to decide where to start. Everything posted
# after it gets processed; everything before it is ignored, so this is how you
# avoid walking years of history. Once state/cursor.json exists, this is never
# read again — change the cursor file, not this.
#
# Leave it empty and the first run starts from the channel's most recent post.
CURSOR_SEED_MESSAGE_ID=


# --- There is no API key, and there will not be one -------------------------
#
# This project spends nothing. Reading the infographics with a vision model was
# in the original plan and was withdrawn on 8 September 2026 because it needs a
# paid API. If you find a document that asks for ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, it predates
# that decision. See the constraint at the top of CLAUDE.md.
